          %h2#references References
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral General
          %p
            See also the references at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            (
            %a{:href => "cosmology#ReferencesGeneral"}> here
            ).
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthias+Blau"}> Matthias Blau
              , chapter 38 of:
              %em Lecture notes on general relativity
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.blau.itp.unibe.ch/GRLecturenotes.html"}> web
              )
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Jorge L. Cervantes-Cota, George Smoot,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmology today – A brief review
                %strong 1396
                (2011) 28-52 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1107.1789"}> arXiv:1107.1789
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.3647524"} doi:10.1063/1.3647524
            %li#Mukhanov16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Viatcheslav+Mukhanov"}> Viatcheslav Mukhanov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum Universe
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/1507528"} spire:1507528
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3367/UFNe.2016.07.037857/meta"} doi:10.3367/UFNe.2016.07.037857
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/xUIrj_97i0A"} video recording
          %blockquote
            %p In March 2013, following an accurate processing of available measurement data, the Planck Scientific Collaboration published the highest-resolution photograph ever of the early Universe when it was only a few hundred thousand years old. The photograph showed galactic seeds in sufficient detail to test some nontrivial theoretical predictions made more than thirty years ago. Most amazing was that all predictions were confirmed to be remarkably accurate. With no exaggeration, we may consider it established experimentally that quantum physics, which is normally assumed to be relevant on the atomic and subatomic scale, also works on the scale of the entire Universe, determining its structure with all its galaxies, stars, and planets.
          %ul
            %li
              George Efstathiou, Steven Gratton,
              %em The evidence for a spatially flat Universe
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06892"}> arXiv:2002.06892
              )
          %p
            Discussion of open problems (see also at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhomogeneous+cosmology"} inhomogeneous cosmology
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Benoit Famaey, Stacy McGaugh,
                %em Challenges for Lambda-CDM and MOND
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.0623"}> arXiv:1301.0623
                )
            %li#BCKRW15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Buchert"}> Thomas Buchert
                , Alan A. Coley,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hagen+Kleinert"} Hagen Kleinert
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Observational Challenges for the Standard FLRW Model
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.03313"} arXiv:1512.03313
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lambda-CDM_model"} Lambda-CDM model
            %li#Einasto09
              %p
                Jaan Einasto,
                %em Dark matter
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0901.0632"}> arXiv:0901.0632
                ) 2009
          %h3#possible_tension_with_observation Possible tension with observation
          %p
            Possible tensions in the model, regarding determination of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hubble+constant"} Hubble constant
            in the early and late universe, apparently observed by various groups, since the late 2010s:
          %p review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                L. Verde, T. Treu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+G.+Riess"} Adam G. Riess
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tensions between the Early and the Late Universe
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.10625"} arXiv:1907.10625
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41550-019-0902-0"} doi:10.1038/s41550-019-0902-0
            %li#SWP22
              %p
                Snowmass White Paper:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmology Intertwined: A Review of the Particle Physics, Astrophysics, and Cosmology Associated with the Cosmological Tensions and Anomalies
                %strong 34
                (2022) 49-211 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.06142"}> arXiv:2203.06142
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jheap.2022.04.002"} doi:10.1016/j.jheap.2022.04.002
          %p Indication that the tension is not in the data but in systematic errors:
          %ul
            %li
              Freedman et al.
              %em The Carnegie-Chicago Hubble Program. VIII. An Independent Determination of the Hubble Constant Based on the Tip of the Red Giant Branch
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.05922"}> arxiv:1907.05922
              )
          %p
            Indication from new data from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Webb+Space+Telescope"} James Webb Space Telescope
            that the old data does not have systematic errors and the tension is in the data:
          %ul
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord>
                Wenlong Yuan
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Wenlong+Yuan"} ?
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+G.+Riess"} Adam G. Riess
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Stefano Casertano
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Stefano+Casertano"} ?
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Lucas M. Macri
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Lucas+M.+Macri"} ?
              %em A First Look at Cepheids in a SN Ia Host with JWST
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.09101"}> arXiv:2209.09101
              )
          %p
            Review of further observed deviations (such as large-scale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhomogeneous+cosmology"} inhomogeneties
            like the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KBC+void"} KBC void
          %ul
            %li#Peebles22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Phillip+James+E.+Peebles"}> Phillip James E. Peebles
              ,
              %em Anomalies in Physical Cosmology
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.05018"}> arXiv:2208.05018
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            There are possible tensions with high redshift
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/galaxies"} galaxies
            detected at the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Webb+Space+Telescope"} James Webb Space Telescope
          %ul
            %li
              Michael Boylan-Kolchin,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stress Testing ΛCDM with High-redshift Galaxy Candidates
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.01611"} arXiv:2208.01611
          %p
            For testing the standard model of cosmology in light of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Webb+Space+Telescope"} James Webb Space Telescope
          %ul
            %li
              Nikita Lovyagin, Alexander Raikov, Vladimir Yershov, Yuri Lovyagin,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Cosmological Model Tests with JWST
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.06575"} arXiv:2212.06575
          %p
            On the possibility that these tensions could, in part, by a sign/cause of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhomogeneous+cosmology"} inhomogeneous cosmology
            violating the widely assumed “cosmological principle”:
          %ul
            %li
              Pavan Kumar Aluri, et al.,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Is the Observable Universe Consistent with the Cosmological Principle?
              %strong 40
              9 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1361-6382/acbefc"}> doi:10.1088/1361-6382/acbefc
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.05765"} arXiv:2207.05765
          %h3#in_aqft_on_curved_spacetimes In AQFT on Curved spacetimes
          %p
            Discussion in the rigorous context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT+on+curved+spacetimes"} AQFT on curved spacetimes
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"}> Klaus Fredenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas-Paul+Hack"} Thomas-Paul Hack
                %em Quantum field theory on curved spacetime and the standard cosmological model
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.6773"}> arXiv:1308.6773
                )
            %li#Hack13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas-Paul+Hack"}> Thomas-Paul Hack
                ,
                %em The Lambda CDM-model in quantum field theory on curved spacetime and Dark Radiation
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1306.3074"}> arXiv:1306.3074
                )
          %p For review see
          %ul
            %li#Hack15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas-Paul+Hack"}> Thomas-Paul Hack
              , section 3.2.1
              = succeed "," do
                %em Cosmological Applications of Algebraic Quantum Field Theory in Curved Spacetimes
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.01869"} arXiv:1506.01869
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-21894-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-21894-6
        .revisedby
